    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Two historic truss bridges—one built in 1905 and another in 1941—span the Neosho River near New Strawn and are listed on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/strawn-kansas-ghost-town/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Only three original buildings survive from Old Strawn: a historic church, the schoolmaster’s house, and a coal‑weighing foundation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
